  unit: { count: 134, covers: "the pieces each Working Unit added, beside the code: the tally's record encoding, torn-line parsing and per-tip reading (W1); the preflight's one-block refusal and its exempt arm (W2); the note tool's count rule, identity split, renderers and the kinds it refuses (W3); which hash a review note of each schema binds and which note a design verdict is read from (W4); a nit decided by exactly one non-empty disposition (W5); cr/v5 with, without and with a malformed fleet block, and the whole-diff pair closed (W6); a readiness rule stated as a pure function so an exempt tip is signable and a gated one still owes three notes (W7); stage_seconds, the candidate pool and the verifier model, an absent row untimed rather than zero (W8); the code-path subset hash in git.rs; and the check table - the review runs where a note binds a range and never at commit level, a check emitted by another borrowing its levels with resolution one hop deep and acyclic, and the receipt's line asserted literally per level rather than against the table that produced it (W9)" }
  integration: { count: 196, covers: "each Working Unit's bounded contract over a real temp git repo through the real binary: a red gate records its refused ids and a tip its own rounds (W1); malformed, absent and zero-layer notes, an unproven tree, a wrong checkout and uncommitted work each refused in front of the review, an exempt diff never refused, a deferred preflight greening a tree it never measured while still refusing the three cheap things (W2, W8); both notes written from one judgment and left green by the gate's own checks, every derived-field disagreement refused with the gate's ids and nothing written (W3); a doc commit after a PASS keeps the binding and a code commit reds it, a whole-diff cr/v4 refused, a design-only diff owing design/v1 and no review, an artifact rewritten after its verdict voided, the confirm reading a review note the way the gate does (W4); an undecided nit refused by name and a dispositioned one merging (W5); a cr/v5 PASS greening a seam, an epic walk over cr/v2..v5 seams each read at its declared binding, tally --fleet billing the round that counted itself (W6); the gate reading neither the clock nor the pool (W8); a docs-only Working Unit signed and green, a code-bearing one still refused (W7); and the receipt naming the checks its level actually ran, at epic, seam and standalone-commit level (W9)" }
  e2e: { count: 5, covers: "the epic plan's e2e table over one hermetic repo through the real xtask binary, the real merge hook and real git: three Working Units - code beside docs, a closed design run beside code, and a diff that changes no code - each with its notes written by cargo xtask notes write and its review bound to the code paths, land on main; a document after a PASS leaves it standing while a code fix voids it; a design run amended after both verdicts voids only design/v1; a docs-only tip owes no review and is still signable; the walk refuses the epic merge when a seam has lost its review and lands it once restored; and, in a real crate, a failing test and then a malformed note are each refused by the preflight under the gate's own id before any finder would spawn. The manual-review e2e is carried unchanged as the signing flow every one of those seams is gated through" }
